# Regression case 1: deposition onto a solid floor.
#
# Deliberately contact-dominated -- 250 polydisperse prolate spheroids settle
# into a dense layer -- so a change to the force law or the contact geometry
# shows up immediately.  Calibration for the tolerances in check_physics.py:
# recompiling the unchanged source with -O3 -march=native perturbs positions
# by ~1e-12, while scaling the Hertzian force by 1.0001 moves them by ~9e-6.
boxsize		1 1 1.2
boxcorner	0 0 0
density		1
Gravity		0   0   -10
outDt		0.025
timeStep	0.0001
maxTime		0.275
particleSize	0.05
particleSizeWidth 0.05
nParticle	250
stiffness	5e+02
damping		5e+0
friction	2.0e-1
cohesion	0.0
output		out
method		deposition
boundary	solid
eta		1.4
etaWidth	0.25
zeta		1.4
zetaWidth	0.25
